From 65c334c84ee739a1cdccc4b9e948cbe8f9b0d28b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:31:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ryGT: frame generation, shader precompile on the splash
 screen, compile freeze

- Frame generation: AMD FSR 3.1.4 frame generation (amd_fidelityfx_vk.dll, GPU.framegen_enabled).
  FidelityFX makes the swapchain (three extra graphics-family queues), the presenter records its
  per-frame preparation; zero motion vectors and flat depth, as the game gives none. Paced with
  hybrid spin and fence waits. The FPS counter shows game and shown frames.
- PERF-097: shader translation and pipeline build workers run on the efficiency cores.
- PERF-098: GPU.precompile_shaders: every stored pipeline is built while the splash screen shows
  (idle command thread installs them, all workers build them), with a progress bar.
- PERF-100: GPU.compile_freeze: the game pauses (guest clocks held) while a new pipeline
  compiles; the last frame is shown again with a "Compiling new shaders..." notice (bottom left).
  The re-shown frame is taken out of the free queue meanwhile (a crash in the driver otherwise).
- PERF-101: GPU.compile_batch_ms: a compile pause also finishes the read-ahead builds, up to that
  long.
- PERF-102: the game waits on the splash screen until the precompile is done; meanwhile builds
  use every core.
- PERF-095 (opt-in, SHADGT_LAZY_ASC_EPOCH=1): compute-queue upload epochs only when a queue reads
  memory.
- DIAG-097 (opt-in): GT Sport view-distance settings hooks (RYGT_ENV_*); read/write hardware
  watches (DIAG-067 "rw").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
